    "label": "Note body",
    "type": "richtext",
    "required": false,
    "default": "<p>Helena started with a last-chance gold strike in 1864, and my family has worked this valley ever since. Mining teaches a few things that stick: assay the rock before you sell it, respect the people working beside you, and only promise a vein you have actually seen.</p><p>I started SunRiver to build the version I would want as the client. One senior person who scopes the work honestly, names a fixed fee before we start, and hands you everything in your name when we finish. Your domain, your hosting, your code, your logins, all held in your own hands.</p><p>That is the whole pitch. Senior work, a fair number, and a person who picks up the phone. The cats came with the deal, and they work for treats.</p>",
    "id": "10160003-0001-0001-0001-000000000003"
